WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.205
September 24

2
00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.900
Dear Kind Trustee Who Sends Orphans to College,

3
00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:13.149
Well, here I am at college!

4
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.874
I traveled for four hours on the train.

5
00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:24.067
I never rode on a train before.

6
00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:29.395
College is the biggest, most confusing place I've ever been!

7
00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:35.241
I get lost whenever I leave my room.

8
00:00:35.242 --> 00:00:38.965
It seems strange to write letters to someone I don't know.

9
00:00:38.966 --> 00:00:42.429
Actually, it seems strange to be writing letters at all.

10
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.987
I've only written three or four in my life.

11
00:00:45.988 --> 00:00:49.708
So please forgive me if my letters aren't perfect.

12
00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:54.627
Before I left, Mrs. Lippett and I had a very serious talk.

13
00:00:54.628 --> 00:00:58.470
She told me how to behave for the rest of my life.

14
00:00:58.471 --> 00:01:02.090
Including how I should behave toward you.

15
00:01:02.091 --> 00:01:10.083
"Jerusha, you must be very respectful to the kind gentleman who's doing so much for you," she said.

16
00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:15.426
"But how can I be respectful to someone who wants to be called John Smith?

17
00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:18.094
I wish he'd chosen a more interesting name.

18
00:01:18.095 --> 00:01:23.303
I might as well write letters to Dear Hitching Post."

19
00:01:23.304 --> 00:01:28.296
"Jerusha!" Mrs. Lippett was shocked.

20
00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:32.518
"That is not respectful!"

21
00:01:32.519 --> 00:01:36.292
I thought about you a great deal this summer.

22
00:01:36.293 --> 00:01:39.250
You've taken an interest in me.

23
00:01:39.251 --> 00:01:42.777
That makes me almost feel that I have a family. It

24
00:01:42.778 --> 00:01:48.779
seems as if I belong to somebody now, and I like that feeling. But

25
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.507
when I think about you, I have very little to work with. I

26
00:01:53.508 --> 00:01:56.404
only know three things about you: 1.

27
00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:58.824
You are tall. 2.

28
00:01:58.825 --> 00:02:01.300
You are rich. 3.

29
00:02:01.301 --> 00:02:04.145
You hate girls. I

30
00:02:04.146 --> 00:02:11.132
suppose I could address you as Dear Mr. Girl Hater. But that's rather insulting to me. Or

31
00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.380
Dear Mr. Rich Man, but that's insulting to you. That

32
00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:18.702
sounds like money is the only important thing about you. Besides,

33
00:02:18.703 --> 00:02:22.886
maybe you won't stay rich for your whole life. Lots

34
00:02:22.887 --> 00:02:26.818
of wealthy men lose all their money in the stock market. But

35
00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:30.304
at least you'll stay tall all your life! So

36
00:02:30.305 --> 00:02:36.876
I've decided to call you Daddy Longlegs. I hope you won't mind. It's

37
00:02:36.877 --> 00:02:40.442
just a private nickname. Please

38
00:02:40.443 --> 00:02:43.463
don't tell Mrs. Lippett! Let

39
00:02:43.464 --> 00:02:48.411
me tell you about my room, which is in a tower in Fergussen Hall. It

40
00:02:48.412 --> 00:02:54.035
used to be part of the infirmary before the college built the new one. There

41
00:02:54.036 --> 00:02:58.140
are three other girls on the same floor. There's

42
00:02:58.141 --> 00:03:01.168
a senior who wears glasses. She's

43
00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:06.803
always telling us to be quiet. And

44
00:03:06.804 --> 00:03:12.414
two freshmen, Sallie McBride and Julia Rutledge Pendleton. Sallie

45
00:03:12.415 --> 00:03:17.065
has red hair and is quite friendly. Julia

46
00:03:17.066 --> 00:03:21.408
comes from one of the wealthiest families in New York.

47
00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:26.476
She hasn't noticed me yet.

48
00:03:26.477 --> 00:03:33.103
Sallie and Julia room together, but the senior and I have singles.

49
00:03:33.104 --> 00:03:36.103
Usually freshmen can't get singles.

50
00:03:36.104 --> 00:03:39.445
But I got one without even asking.

51
00:03:39.446 --> 00:03:45.046
Maybe the college was worried about my behavior around girls raised by proper families.

52
00:03:45.047 --> 00:03:48.755
So there are advantages to being an orphan!

53
00:03:48.756 --> 00:03:51.573
I'm going to enjoy my own room.

54
00:03:51.574 --> 00:03:58.012
Especially after spending 18 years in one room with 20 roommates!

55
00:03:58.013 --> 00:04:06.068
Sallie is the most entertaining person in the world, and Julia is the least entertaining person.

56
00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:11.268
Sallie thinks everything is funny, and Julia is bored with everything.

57
00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:15.623
Julia never makes the slightest effort to be friendly.

58
00:04:15.624 --> 00:04:21.476
She believes that if you're born a Pendleton, you deserve only the best things.

59
00:04:21.477 --> 00:04:25.980
She and I were born to be enemies!

60
00:04:25.981 --> 00:04:28.837
I've fixed up my room with Sallie's help.

61
00:04:28.838 --> 00:04:35.501
She has lived in a real house all her life, so I trusted her advice.

62
00:04:35.502 --> 00:04:39.308
"Let's go to the senior auction," she said the other day.

63
00:04:39.309 --> 00:04:43.300
"The seniors will be selling things they don't want anymore."

64
00:04:43.301 --> 00:04:48.101
When we got to the auction, I had no idea where to begin. But

65
00:04:48.102 --> 00:04:51.464
Sallie steered me toward a wooden desk. "You

66
00:04:51.465 --> 00:04:57.130
should bid on that. It's very nice." "What

67
00:04:57.131 --> 00:05:02.904
about that brown rug over there?" I said. But

68
00:05:02.905 --> 00:05:06.901
when we looked at it, we noticed an ink spot. "The

69
00:05:06.902 --> 00:05:12.720
ink spot will make it less expensive." Sallie looked around. "And

70
00:05:12.721 --> 00:05:17.794
with the money you save, you could buy that wicker chair. Then

71
00:05:17.795 --> 00:05:21.682
you could put the chair over the spot." So

72
00:05:21.683 --> 00:05:27.642
I bought all three items as well as some yellow curtains and cushions. You

73
00:05:27.643 --> 00:05:34.242
can't imagine how fun it is to shop, and get change back after paying! Especially

74
00:05:34.243 --> 00:05:38.386
since I've never had more than a few cents in my life. I

75
00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:44.191
assure you, Daddy dear, I do appreciate the allowance. Well,

76
00:05:44.192 --> 00:05:49.278
it's time for me to end my first letter. One more thing . . . Sallie

77
00:05:49.279 --> 00:05:51.720
just poked her head in my door. She

78
00:05:51.721 --> 00:05:59.130
said, "I'm so homesick that I simply can't stand it. Do you feel that way?" I

79
00:05:59.131 --> 00:06:07.089
smiled a little. "No, I think I'll be all right." I've

80
00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.652
never heard of anyone being orphanage sick . Have you?

81
00:06:11.653 --> 00:06:14.138
Yours most respectfully,

82
00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:19.421
Jerusha Abbott

